<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grattan's Parliament</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1782">1782</a>–<a href="/years/1800">1800</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Grattan's Parliament is the name given to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parliament-of-ireland">Irish Parliament</a> between 1782 and 1800, after it won legislative independence from Westminster through the repeal of the Declaratory Act and changes to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poynings-law">Poynings' Law</a>. Named after the patriot leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-grattan">Henry Grattan</a>, it remained an assembly of the Protestant Ascendancy. It voted itself out of existence in the Acts of Union, which took effect in 1801.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/grattans-parliament.jpg" alt="Grattan's Parliament" width="320" height="406" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: http://www.geographicus.com/mm5/cartographers/rocque.txt · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1794_Rocque_Wall_Map_of_Ireland_-_Geographicus_-_Ireland2-rocque-1794.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
